---
// The main prediction path, arranged vertically so it remains readable on a
// phone. Keep auxiliary heads and recycling in notes rather than crossing
// their routes through the first-pass overview.
---
<figure class="af2-arch-fig" aria-labelledby="af2-overview-title">
  <header class="af2-heading">
    <span class="af2-kicker">THE FULL MODEL</span>
    <h4 id="af2-overview-title">From sequence information to atom coordinates</h4>
    <p>Follow the main prediction path from top to bottom.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="af2-stage">
    <div class="af2-stage-heading"><span>01</span><strong><a href="#2-input-representations">Prepare the inputs</a></strong><small>§§2, 8</small></div>
    <div class="af2-inputs">
      <div><strong>Target sequence</strong><span>The protein to predict</span></div>
      <div><strong>MSA</strong><span>Aligned related sequences</span></div>
      <div><strong>Templates</strong><span>Available structural hints</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="af2-detail">Input embedding, extra-MSA processing, and template processing build two working representations.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="af2-two-streams">
    <div class="af2-handoff af2-msa"><span class="af2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><strong>MSA representation <i>m</i></strong><span>Sequences × residues</span></div>
    <div class="af2-handoff af2-pair"><span class="af2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><strong>Pair representation <i>z</i></strong><span>Residues × residues</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="af2-stage af2-evoformer">
    <div class="af2-stage-heading"><span>02</span><strong><a href="#3-the-evoformer--birds-eye-view">Evoformer</a></strong><small>48 blocks · §§3–7</small></div>
    <div class="af2-two-streams af2-updates">
      <div class="af2-msa"><strong>Update <i>m</i></strong><span>Read evolutionary patterns</span></div>
      <div class="af2-pair"><strong>Update <i>z</i></strong><span>Refine residue-pair features</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="af2-detail">The streams exchange information through pair-biased attention and the outer product mean.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="af2-two-streams">
    <div class="af2-handoff af2-msa"><span class="af2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><strong>Target row of <i>m</i> → single <i>s</i></strong><span>Select the first row, then project it</span></div>
    <div class="af2-handoff af2-pair"><span class="af2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><strong>Refined pair <i>z</i></strong><span>Pass the full pair representation</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="af2-stage af2-structure">
    <div class="af2-stage-heading"><span>03</span><strong><a href="#10-the-structure-module">Structure Module</a></strong><small>8 iterations · §10</small></div>
    <p class="af2-detail">Use <i>s</i> and <i>z</i> to update residue frames and predict side-chain geometry.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="af2-result"><span class="af2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><strong>3D atom coordinates</strong></div>

  <figcaption>
    <strong>One forward pass.</strong> Only the target row of <i>m</i> enters the Structure Module.
    The other MSA rows have already influenced both the target row and the pair representation.
    <a href="#9-recycling">Recycling</a> feeds the final target row, pair features, and coordinate-derived distances
    into another pass (§9). Confidence and distance predictions use <a href="#11-auxiliary-heads">separate heads (§11)</a>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .af2-arch-fig { margin: 1.75rem 0; padding: 1.35rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: .7rem; background: var(--surface-strong); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .af2-heading { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .af2-kicker { color: var(--accent); font: 600 .65rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .af2-heading h4 { margin: .4rem 0 .35rem; color: var(--fg); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .af2-heading p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  .af2-stage { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: .5rem; background: var(--bg); padding: 1rem; }
  .af2-stage-heading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .af2-stage-heading > span { color: var(--accent); font: .7rem var(--font-mono); }
  .af2-stage-heading strong { font-size: .95rem; color: var(--fg); }
  .af2-stage-heading small { margin-left: auto; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .7rem; }
  .af2-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .6rem; }
  .af2-inputs > div { padding: .65rem .75rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: .35rem; background: var(--surface-strong); }
  .af2-inputs strong, .af2-inputs span, .af2-handoff strong, .af2-handoff > span:not(.af2-arrow), .af2-updates strong, .af2-updates span { display: block; }
  .af2-inputs strong { color: var(--fg); font-size: .78rem; }
  .af2-inputs span { margin-top: .25rem; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .7rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .af2-detail { margin: .65rem 0 0; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .af2-two-streams { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .85rem; }
  .af2-msa { --stream: var(--data-msa); }
  .af2-pair { --stream: var(--data-pair); }
  .af2-handoff { padding: .25rem .4rem .9rem; text-align: center; }
  .af2-arrow { display: block; font-size: 1.4rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--stream, var(--data-structure)); }
  .af2-handoff strong { color: var(--stream); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .af2-handoff > span:not(.af2-arrow) { margin-top: .2rem; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .69rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .af2-updates > div { padding: .65rem .8rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--stream); border-radius: .2rem; background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--stream) 8%, var(--surface-strong)); }
  .af2-updates strong { color: var(--stream); font-size: .8rem; }
  .af2-updates span { margin-top: .2rem; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .73rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .af2-structure { border-color: var(--data-structure); background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--data-structure) 6%, var(--bg)); }
  .af2-structure .af2-stage-heading { margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  .af2-structure .af2-detail { margin: 0; }
  .af2-result { text-align: center; padding-bottom: .85rem; color: var(--data-structure); font-size: .9rem; }
  .af2-arch-fig figcaption { margin: .1rem 0 0; padding-top: .9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: .76rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .af2-arch-fig figcaption strong { color: var(--fg); }
  .af2-arch-fig a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 45%, var(--rule)); text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  .af2-arch-fig a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: currentColor; }
  .af2-arch-fig a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: .1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .af2-arch-fig { padding: 1rem .8rem; }
    .af2-stage { padding: .8rem; }
    .af2-inputs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .4rem; }
    .af2-inputs > div { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: .75rem; padding: .55rem; }
    .af2-inputs span { margin: 0; text-align: right; }
    .af2-stage-heading small { font-size: .65rem; }
    .af2-two-streams { gap: .5rem; }
    .af2-handoff strong { font-size: .76rem; }
  }
</style>
